# Pstack

Read `.cursor/skills/pstack/<name>/SKILL.md` before citing it. Cite only what you read.

The vendored snapshot is `.cursor/skills/pstack/`. Update it only with `scripts/sync-pstack.sh <source-dir>`.

## Decision table

| Task type | pstack sequence |
|---|---|
| Bug fix | poteto-mode Bug fix playbook: reproduce on the real surface, then why (regression history) or how, then binary-search with runtime evidence, then architect if the fix crosses a boundary, then failing repro before the fix (sequence-verifiable-units), then prove-it-works on the same surface |
| New feature | how, then foundational-thinking (data shape), then architect (with arena inside), then implement in verifiable units, then prove-it-works (verify-<app> skill if it exists) |
| Refactor or migration | how, then why if layering changes, then laziness-protocol and subtract first, then figure-it-out for a large one, then sequence-verifiable-units with per-unit checks, then blast-radius |
| Perf work | benchmark-checklist on the baseline, then Perf issue or Hillclimb playbook, then one change per measurement, then benchmark-checklist again before reporting any number |
| Design decision | how, then why, then architect (2 or more designs through arena), and an opt-in checkpoint only on a one-way door |
| Risky change (image Jacob will deploy, prod data) | blast-radius (prove the safety fact by running it), then prove-it-works, and Hans approves only truly irreversible steps |
| Repeated correction | correct: add a rule row, enforce it at the highest level, and prove the check fails on the past mistake |
| Explaining code | how (what it does) or why (motivation), then bro if Hans needs it in plain words |
| Delegating (CLI review, Cloud agent) | the delegation contract (section 2b), with skills named per row above, then judge the returned evidence, and reject work that has none |
| Long or unattended run | figure-it-out plus show-me-your-work |

## Evidence a PR must return

Return all of the following or the work is rejected:

1. Commit SHA(s) and branch, plus the PR URL it landed on.
2. The exact commands run and their verbatim output (failing then passing for each check), with the Actions run URLs.
3. For any number: run count, median, range, limiter (benchmark-checklist).
4. Verdict VERIFIED / NOT VERIFIED / INCONCLUSIVE against the predicate, and what is still unproven.
5. Deviations from the plan, each with its reason.

Put that evidence in the PR body's `## Verification` section. Fill `Predicate:`, `Commands:`, `Output:`, and `Verdict:`. CI `pr-evidence` fails while any of those four is empty or still a placeholder.
